## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design and analyze dynamic constraint propagation with 3-valued domains, going beyond static logic. The problem requires constructing a concrete propagation trace and a fixed point that preserves an unknown value, mirroring real-world policy engines.

## Key Concepts
- Forward-propagation with 3-valued domains
- Fixed-point convergence
- Handling U without monotone destruction
- Traceable propagation: demonstrate steps and termination

## Code Example
```javascript
function applyRules(state){
  // state: {X1,X2,X3,X4} values in {T,F,U}
  // R1
  if(state.X1==="T" && state.X2==="T") state.X3="T";
  // R2
  if(state.X4==="F") state.X1="F";
  // R3
  if(state.X3==="F") {
    if(state.X2!=="F" && state.X4!=="F") { /* no change */ }
  }
  // R4
  if(state.X1==="U" || state.X2==="U") state.X4="U";
  return state;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you detect non-termination or oscillation in this system?
- How would you extend to ensure a fixed point with at least one U is reachable from any initial state?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to reason with Kleene 3-valued semantics in a concrete constraint system, plus practical propagation and backtracking.

## Key Concepts
- Kleene 3-valued logic: T>U>F; ¬U=U; a→b = (¬a) ∨ b; ∨/∧ as max/min.
- Constraint propagation: prune inconsistent values; arc-consistency.
- Backtracking: search space pruning when a constraint becomes F.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Kleene 3-valued semantics helpers (T=1, U=0.5, F=0)
const V = { T: 1, U: 0.5, F: 0 };
const notV = (v) => (v === V.T ? V.F : v === V.F ? V.T : V.U);
const orV = (a,b) => Math.max(a,b);
const andV = (a,b) => Math.min(a,b);
const implies = (a,b) => orV(notV(a), b);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- Extend to five sensors with additional constraints and analyze the complexity.
- Compare forward-only propagation vs. combined forward-backward strategies under Kleene semantics.

## Why This Is Asked
Tests 3-valued dataflow reasoning, fixpoint propagation, and translating logic into a workable algorithm.

## Key Concepts
- Kleene three-valued logic (T, F, U)
- Worklist/fixpoint propagation
- Dataflow dependency graphs
- Handling cycles and convergence

## Code Example
```javascript
// Kleene 3-valued logic
const T = true, F = false, U = 'U';
function not(x){ if (x===T) return F; if (x===F) return T; return U; }
function and(a,b){ if (a===F || b===F) return F; if (a===T && b===T) return T; return U; }
function or(a,b){ if (a===T || b===T) return T; if (a===F && b===F) return F; return U; }

// program: A = B AND C; D = NOT E; F = D OR A
let B = U, C = T, E = U;
let A = and(B, C);
let D = not(E);
let F = or(D, A);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend to cycles and determine worst-case iterations?
- How would you optimize for sparse graphs and pruning impossible combinations?

## Why This Is Asked
